      "statusChangeID": "6a4e7c6166755f1cfa9ca886",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "needs more information",
      "value": "@{61af182f59e34c4a9fca46ec|full_name} I am assuming this is your world. Can you check in editor how you configured those trees? Prior to Unity 6, scale for Terrain trees was only set as the `_TreeInstanceScale` property on the shader, never applied directly to the transform. Now, the engine checks if that property exists first. If the Material does *not* have that property, it will apply scale directly. If this is something you can fix on your end, we would prefer to leave the fix in for Unity 6, as otherwise it'd desync again as soon as we provide a U6-based SDK.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
